cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PyIMR: fast, validated solvers for inertial microcavitation rheometry"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bryngelson
    given-names: Spencer
    email: sbryngelson@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/sbryngelson/PyIMR"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21792446
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - cavitation
  - rheometry
  - bubble dynamics
  - inverse problems
  - jax
abstract: >-
  Solvers for inertial microcavitation rheometry with a typed, dimensional material API,
  built for inference campaigns that need many forward evaluations. Covers six radial
  equations, bubble and medium thermal transport, vapour transport, and closed-form,
  composable and distributed constitutive models. Includes forward sensitivities through
  the production right-hand side, Bayesian constitutive model selection, and resolution
  and conditioning diagnostics measured on the caller's own problem rather than assumed.
